From 0513f16ca2f3ed070613b1cb04768d629b215256 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:29:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] language: no lone msgstr at the end of the core strings

The last block of the core catalogue of English was a msgstr "" that belonged to no entry. It was
left there when the two strings of "Keep the graphics card at full speed while HD audio plays
through" were put in before the msgstr of the entry that ended the file. Kodi's parser skips a
block without a msgid (CPODocument::GetNextEntry()), so no string was lost, but gettext does not
take the file (msgfmt -c: syntax error), nor would any tool that reads it as a catalogue.

Now every block of the catalogue has its msgctxt, msgid and msgstr, and msgfmt -c takes it.
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index 3e97f68..3a686cb 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -27520,5 +27520,3 @@ msgstr ""
 msgctxt "#41800"
 msgid "The list of this folder could not be read to its end ({}). Some of its files may be missing, so nothing is shown. This usually means that the disk or its file system is damaged: check the disk."
 msgstr ""
-
-msgstr ""
-- 
2.53.0

